    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #361\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed commit `b3669f6` to branch `bb/relay-150-notifications-v1-03-05-manage-session-thr_z3bt4hp9fu`, updating the existing pull request #361.\n\nCloses #150\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #150: session-bound push registrations.\n\n- **Migration `0031_push_subscriptions.sql`**: `push_subscriptions` table (user, nullable session, `channel` web_push/apns, platform, web fields, APNs fields, timestamps, `revoked_at`), with CHECK constraints enforcing channel/field and channel/platform validity, plus partial unique indexes on `endpoint`/`device_token` scoped to active (non-revoked) rows.\n- **`push/` data package**: upsert-based registration (reactivates a revoked row as a fresh active row via `ON CONFLICT` matching the partial unique index), scoped explicit revocation, session-cascade revocation, and one repository operation (`revokePushSubscriptionByProviderInvalidation`) — all required directly by issue #150's Task section, not deferred work for a later issue.\n- **`authActions.ts`**: `logout` and `revokeUserSession` now cascade into push-registration revocation in the same transaction, so a registration never outlives its session while other sessions keep working.\n- **HTTP surface**: `POST /api/push-subscriptions` (register/reactivate) and `POST /api/push-subscriptions/:id/revoke`, authenticated the same way as every other protected route, wired into `app.ts` and documented in `routeMatrix.ts`. The request-body parser rejects non-object JSON (e.g. a literal `null`) with a 400 instead of crashing into a 500.\n\nThis round addressed CI review feedback on PR #361: clarified the `revokePushSubscriptionByProviderInvalidation` docstring to state plainly that it's part of #150's own required scope, removing a misleading reference to a future issue that had caused the automated reviewer to flag it as speculative generality.\n\nVerified this run: unit tests 127/127, integration tests 849/849 (real ephemeral Postgres), e2e tests 5/5, ESLint clean repo-wide, `tsc --noEmit` clean across all packages/services, Prettier clean repo-wide, dependency-boundaries check clean.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
